CLI.md §3.4: --target accepts only go, cpp, ts, json or view.
-- args --
build
--target
foo
-- want --
[exit 2]
[stdout]
[stderr]
canon: invalid value "foo" for flag -target: "foo": want go, cpp, ts, json or view
usage: canon <command> [arguments] [flags]

commands:
  build [packages...]   check, then write the outputs of packages
  check [packages...]   parse and check packages, print findings
  edit [request.json]   apply an edit request (JSON) from the file or stdin
  explain <path>        print a value, its type and where each part was set
  fmt [paths...]        rewrite sources in the canonical layout
  guide [topic]         print the agent guide: the index, or one topic
  init                  create project.canon in the current directory
  lock check [pkgs...]  verify canon.lock against the sources, no build
  lsp                   run the language server on stdin and stdout
  new <package>         create a package directory with a first file
  refs <path>           list every place that references an entry or member
  rename <name> <new>   rename a Canon name and everything that names it
  test [packages...]    run the test blocks of packages
  version               print the compiler, language and format versions

flags:
  -adopt path
    	take over the hand-written file at path (repeatable)
  -check
    	write nothing; exit 1 if any output or lock would change
  -color when
    	colour text output: when is auto, always or never (auto: a terminal, unless NO_COLOR is set) (default "auto")
  -format format
    	output format: text or json (default "text")
  -lang code
    	code of the language of translated check messages (default: the source language)
  -layer name
    	apply the layer name; repeatable, applied in order
  -max-warnings n
    	exit with code 4 when there are more than n warnings
  -project string
    	project root (default: search upward from the current directory)
  -q	print errors only
  -quiet
    	print errors only
  -root name=dir
    	use name=dir for a declared root; repeatable
  -target target
    	emit only this target (go, cpp, ts, json, view); repeatable
  -watch
    	run again after every change, printing what changed
